  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-285776" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable livelihood and food security for poor rural communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MONLAR (Movement for Land and Agricultural Reform) has been working for over 20 years to form a broad people&apos;s movement in Sri Lanka bringing together all relevant people&apos;s organisations and sections of society, particularly those sections such as the rural people, plantation communities, fishworkers, labourers, women and young people to challenge top-down policies formulated without their participation, and develop alternative approaches designed to be both equitable and ecologically sustainable.  The core target group is small-scale food producers and their families.  In particular MONLAR seeks to build and empower independent farmer organisations; defend the rights of small-scale food producers to the sustainable use of natural resources; promote healthy lifestyles, good nutrition and improved rural incomes and general quality of life; and to encourage ecologically-friendly farming methods, reclamation of drought-affected or otherwise damaged land, and home gardening.</narrative>
  </description>
